  "answer_text": "Great question \u2014 \"doge\" is actually one of the internet's most debated pronunciations, similar to the GIF controversy! Here's a full breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## How to Pronounce \"Doge\"\n\nThere are **three common pronunciations**, and there's genuine debate over which is \"correct\":\n\n### 1. \ud83c\udfc6 **\"Dohj\"** \u2014 /do\u028a\u0292/ (Most widely accepted for the meme)\nThe most widely accepted pronunciation of Doge (as in the meme/Dogecoin) is **\"dohj\"**, written as /do\u028a\u0292/ in the International Phonetic Alphabet. This pronunciation was confirmed by Dogecoin's co-creator Jackson Palmer, who said the name was inspired by the animated series *Homestar Runner*, where a character spells out D-O-G-E and another character reads it as \"dohj.\"\n\n### 2. **\"Doje\"** \u2014 /do\u028ad\u0292/ (like \"dodge\" but with a long O)\nLanguage columnist Ben Zimmer stated, \"In deference to Strong Bad, I would favor /do\u028a\u0292/ or /do\u028ad\u0292/ (with the J sound).\" Many people default to this one because it feels natural in English.\n\n### 3. **\"Dohg\"** \u2014 /do\u028a\u0261/ (like \"dog\" with a long O)\nSome argue that a dog, if it could speak, \"would pronounce dog with an overemphasized vowel\" \u2014 making it sound like **\"dogue\"** (rhymes with *vogue*).\n\n---\n\n## So which is actually correct?\n\nAccording to Wikipedia, the meme can be pronounced /do\u028a\u0292/, /do\u028ad\u0292/, or /do\u028a\u0261/.\n\nAs with GIF, both the hard G (like \"dog\") and the soft G (because Strong Bad said so) are in common use and can be justified with reasonable explanations.\n\nThe **creator-endorsed** pronunciation is **\"dohj\"** (/do\u028a\u0292/), so if you want to say it the way it was intended, go with that. But honestly, like GIF, people say it differently and there's no single universally enforced answer!\n\n---\n\n**TL;DR:**\n| Pronunciation | Sounds like | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| /do\u028a\u0292/ | \"dohj\" | \u2705 Creator-endorsed, most common in media |\n| /do\u028ad\u0292/ | \"doje\" (like dodge) | Very common, widely accepted |\n| /do\u028a\u0261/ | \"dohg\" (rhymes with vogue) | Less common but used |",
